latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the Input Grid:\n   a. Identify distinct color groups, excluding black (0).\n   b. For each color group, determine its bounding box (min/max row and column).\n   c. Identify the pattern type for each color group (e.g., vertical line, horizontal line, block, scattered).\n   d. Calculate the prominence (ratio of colored cells to total cells in its bounding box) for each color group.\n\n2. Vertical Compression:\n   a. For each color group, compress vertical repetitions by identifying the unique vertical patterns.\n   b. Create a compressed representation of each color group that fits within 3 rows.\n\n3. Shape Idealization:\n   a. For each compressed color group, apply idealization rules:\n      - Complete partial shapes (e.g., L to cross, F to E)\n      - Enhance symmetry where possible\n      - Maintain the general structure and characteristics of the original shape\n   b. Ensure the idealized shape still fits within 3 rows.\n\n4. Horizontal Arrangement:\n   a. Create an empty 3xN output grid, where N is the number of columns in the input.\n   b. Place each idealized shape into the output grid, maintaining their relative horizontal positions from the input.\n   c. If shapes overlap, resolve conflicts by considering:\n      - The prominence of each shape\n      - The original horizontal spread of the shape\n      - The need to maintain distinguishable features of each shape\n\n5. Space Optimization:\n   a. Minimize black (0) spaces between shapes while maintaining necessary separation.\n   b. Ensure that each shape has at least one column of separation from adjacent shapes, unless they were originally adjacent.\n\n6. Vertical Alignment:\n   a. For each column in the output grid:\n      - Move non-zero values to the top\n      - Fill in gaps to complete vertical lines if appropriate\n      - Ensure the column uses all 3 rows if it contains any non-zero values\n\n7. Final Refinement:\n   a. Check for any partial patterns that can be completed within the 3-row constraint.\n   b. Ensure symmetry of shapes where possible without altering their essential characteristics.\n   c. Verify that all colors used in the output are present in the input.\n\n8. Validation:\n   a. Confirm that the output grid is exactly 3 rows tall.\n   b. Verify that the output has the same number of columns as the input.\n   c. Check that the relative horizontal positioning of shapes is maintained from input to output.\n   d. Ensure that each distinct color group from the input is represented in the output.\n\n9. Create Output:\n   a. Construct a new ColoredGrid object with the final 3xN array.\n   b. Return this ColoredGrid as the solution.\n\nThis plan addresses the key aspects identified in our reflection: vertical compression, shape completion and idealization, pattern preservation, and adherence to the 3-row constraint. It should be flexible enough to handle the various input patterns seen in the examples while producing consistent, idealized outputs that capture the essence of the input shapes."
